# RabbitMQ, Saga Pattern & Outbox Pattern – Interview Notes

---

# 🐰 1. RabbitMQ in Microservices

## 📌 What is RabbitMQ?

RabbitMQ is a message broker used for **asynchronous communication** between microservices.

* Based on AMQP protocol
* Uses Queue system
* Decouples services

---

## 📌 Why RabbitMQ?

* Avoid direct service-to-service calls
* Improves scalability
* Reliable message delivery
* Supports async processing

---

## 📌 Architecture

Producer → Exchange → Queue → Consumer

---

## 📌 Your Project Flow (IMPORTANT)

Basket Service → sends event → RabbitMQ → Order Service consumes

Example:
User Checkout → Basket Service → Publish Event → Order Service creates order

---

## 📌 EVENT CONTRACT (Shared Library)

```csharp id="ev1"
public class BasketCheckoutEvent
{
    public string UserName { get; set; }
    public decimal TotalPrice { get; set; }
}
```

---

## 📌 PRODUCER (Basket Service)

```csharp id="ev2"
public async Task Checkout(BasketCheckoutEvent eventMessage)
{
    await _publishEndpoint.Publish(eventMessage);
}
```

---

## 📌 CONSUMER (Order Service)

```csharp id="ev3"
public class BasketCheckoutConsumer : IConsumer<BasketCheckoutEvent>
{
    public async Task Consume(ConsumeContext<BasketCheckoutEvent> context)
    {
        var message = context.Message;

        // Create Order
        Console.WriteLine($"Order created for {message.UserName}");
    }
}
```

---

## 📌 REGISTER RABBITMQ (MassTransit)

```csharp id="ev4"
builder.Services.AddMassTransit(config =>
{
    config.AddConsumer<BasketCheckoutConsumer>();

    config.UsingRabbitMq((ctx, cfg) =>
    {
        cfg.Host("rabbitmq://localhost");

        cfg.ReceiveEndpoint("basketcheckout-queue", e =>
        {
            e.ConfigureConsumer<BasketCheckoutConsumer>(ctx);
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 📌 Advantages

* Async communication
* Loose coupling
* Scalable
* Reliable messaging

---

## 📌 Interview One-Liner

"RabbitMQ enables asynchronous, decoupled communication between microservices using message queues."

